<title>BELGIUM: BBL takes full control of Locabel.</title>
<headline>BBL takes full control of Locabel.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgium's Banque Bruxelles Lambert said on Thursday it had bought the 25 percent of leasing company Locabel that it did not already own from Japan's ORIX Corporation, giving it full control.</p>
<p>No financial details of the deal were disclosed.</p>
<p>Locabel, created in 1961, is the oldest leasing company in continental Europe and the leader in its field in Belgium.</p>
<p>At the end of last year it had a portfolio worth more than 30 billion francs and a net profit of 191.8 million.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
